          "hidden": true
        }
      ],
      "arrows": [],
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 1,
          "show": [
            "st",
            "st2",
            "st3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "show": [
            "li",
            "li3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 3,
          "show": [
            "re",
            "re3",
            "re4"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "There are three kinds of probe, and what matters most is what happens when each one fails."
        },
        {
          "text": "The startup probe asks whether the app has finished starting. Until it passes, the other two wait. If it never passes, the container is restarted."
        },
        {
          "text": "The liveness probe asks whether the process is stuck beyond repair. If it fails, the container is restarted."
        },
        {
          "text": "The readiness probe asks whether the pod should get traffic right now. If it fails, the pod is taken out of the Service, and nothing restarts.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "yaml",
      "type": "code",
      "file": "manifests/base/golinks-deployment.yaml",
      "range": [
        33,
        56
      ],
      "highlights": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "lines": [
            35,
            40
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "lines": [
            41,
            48
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "lines": [
            49,
            56
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 3,
          "lines": [
            37,
            37
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 4,
          "lines": [
            51,
            51
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Here they are in our Deployment. Startup checks healthz every 2 seconds and allows 30 misses: a full minute to start.",
          "senses": {
            "minute": "time"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Liveness checks the same healthz every 10 seconds, waits 2 seconds for an answer, and acts after 3 misses: about 30 seconds."
        },
        {
          "text": "Readiness checks readyz every 5 seconds, and acts after 2 misses: about 10 seconds."
        },
        {
          "text": "The paths differ on purpose. healthz answers only for the process itself."
        },
        {
          "text": "readyz also checks the database with a quick query, because no request can succeed without it.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "stop-db",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "~/k8s-videos",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "kubectl scale statefulset postgres -n golinks --replicas=0",
          "output": [
            "statefulset.apps/postgres scaled"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "command": "kubectl get pods -n golinks",
          "output": [
            "NAME                       READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE",
            "golinks-5f8b6c7d9d-k4xzt   0/1     Running   0          21m",
            "golinks-5f8b6c7d9d-p2rnm   0/1     Running   0          21m"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 3,
          "command": "kubectl describe pod golinks-5f8b6c7d9d-k4xzt -n golinks | grep Unhealthy",
          "output": [
            "  Warning  Unhealthy  2s (x4 over 17s)  kubelet  Readiness probe failed: HTTP probe failed with statuscode: 503"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Let's watch readiness work. We take the database away by scaling Postgres to zero."
        },
        {
          "text": "Within seconds, both API pods show zero of one ready."
        },
        {
          "text": "But look at RESTARTS: still zero. Nothing inside the pods is broken, so nothing is restarted.",
          "say": "But look at restarts: still zero. Nothing inside the pods is broken, so nothing is restarted."
        },
        {
          "text": "The events say why: readyz answered 503, the app's way of saying it can't reach its database.",
          "say": "The events say why: ready Z answered with a five oh three, the app's way of saying it can't reach its database.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "out-of-service",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "~/k8s-videos",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "kubectl describe endpointslices -n golinks | grep -E 'Addr|Ready'",
          "output": [
            "  - Addresses:  10.42.1.15",
            "      Ready:    false",
            "  - Addresses:  10.42.2.9",
            "      Ready:    false"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "command": "curl -i http://go.corp.internal/standup",
          "output": [
            "HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found",
            "Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8",
            "X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff",
            "Date: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 14:52:31 GMT",
            "Content-Length: 19",
            "",
            "404 page not found"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "The Service's EndpointSlice still lists both pods, but marks each one not ready, so the Service sends them nothing."
        },
        {
          "text": "From outside, the request now gets Traefik's plain 404, the same one we saw in Episode 5 when no rule matched."
        },
        {
          "text": "You might expect a 503. But Traefik leaves out any route whose Service has no ready pods, so no rule matches.",
          "say": "You might expect a five oh three. But Traefik leaves out any route whose Service has no ready pods, so no rule matches."
        },
        {
          "text": "Every pod is out because they all share one database. That's correct: without it, there's nothing useful they could do.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "db-back",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "~/k8s-videos",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "kubectl scale statefulset postgres -n golinks --replicas=1",
          "output": [
            "statefulset.apps/postgres scaled"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "command": "kubectl get pods -n golinks",
          "output": [
            "NAME                       READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE",
            "golinks-5f8b6c7d9d-k4xzt   1/1     Running   0          22m",
            "golinks-5f8b6c7d9d-p2rnm   1/1     Running   0          22m",
            "postgres-0                 1/1     Running   0          24s"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 3,
          "command": "curl -i http://go.corp.internal/standup",
          "output": [
            "HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found",
            "Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8",
            "Date: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 14:53:40 GMT",
            "Content-Length: 41",
            "",
            "<p>No link named <b>standup</b> yet.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Now bring the database back."
        },
        {
          "text": "Postgres starts, the next readiness checks pass, and both pods are back in the Service, still with zero restarts."
        },
        {
          "text": "Postgres still has its data, too: scaling to zero left its volume alone."
        },
        {
          "text": "And the request reaches our app again.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "why-not-db",
      "type": "diagram",
      "title": "Why liveness skips the database",
      "boxes": [
