            "n2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 3,
          "focus": [],
          "tone": {
            "g1": "good",
            "g2": "good"
          }
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "That demo also shows why liveness must not check the database."
        },
        {
          "text": "If healthz had failed too, the kubelet would have restarted both pods, over and over, for as long as the database was down."
        },
        {
          "text": "A restart can't fix a database. It only adds startup work and noise, right when things are already going wrong."
        },
        {
          "text": "So liveness checks only what a restart can fix: the process itself.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "freeze",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "admin@k3s-agent-1",
      "prompt": "$",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 1,
          "command": "pgrep -x golinks",
          "output": [
            "48211"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 2,
          "command": "sudo kill -STOP 48211",
          "output": []
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "What can a restart fix? A process that's stuck: a deadlock, say, or a loop that never ends."
        },
        {
          "text": "We can fake one. On the node that runs one of our pods, we find the app's process,"
        },
        {
          "text": "and pause it with a stop signal. It's still there, and its port is still open, but it will never answer again.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "freeze-watch",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "~/k8s-videos",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "kubectl get pod golinks-5f8b6c7d9d-k4xzt -n golinks -w",
          "output": [
            "NAME                       READY   STATUS    RESTARTS     AGE",
            "golinks-5f8b6c7d9d-k4xzt   1/1     Running   0            24m",
            "golinks-5f8b6c7d9d-k4xzt   0/1     Running   0            24m",
            "golinks-5f8b6c7d9d-k4xzt   0/1     Running   1 (1s ago)   25m",
            "golinks-5f8b6c7d9d-k4xzt   1/1     Running   1 (5s ago)   25m"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Back on our machine, we watch that pod."
        },
        {
          "text": "About 10 seconds in, readiness gives up first. The pod leaves the Service, and the other pod takes all the traffic."
        },
        {
          "text": "Liveness needs three misses in a row, 10 seconds apart. Then the kubelet kills the container and starts a new one, and RESTARTS goes to 1.",
          "say": "Liveness needs three misses in a row, 10 seconds apart. Then the kubelet kills the container and starts a new one, and restarts goes to one."
        },
        {
          "text": "The new process passes its probes, and the pod is ready again. Nobody had to step in.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "freeze-why",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "~/k8s-videos",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "kubectl describe pod golinks-5f8b6c7d9d-k4xzt -n golinks | grep -E 'Liveness|Killing'",
          "output": [
            "  Warning  Unhealthy  52s (x3 over 72s)  kubelet  Liveness probe failed: Get \"http://10.42.1.15:8080/healthz\": context deadline exceeded (Client.Timeout exceeded while awaiting headers)",
            "  Normal   Killing    52s                kubelet  Container golinks failed liveness probe, will be restarted"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 1,
          "command": "kubectl logs golinks-5f8b6c7d9d-k4xzt -n golinks --previous --tail=2",
          "output": [
            "{\"time\":\"2026-11-02T14:55:05Z\",\"level\":\"DEBUG\",\"msg\":\"GET /readyz\",\"status\":200,\"ms\":1}",
            "{\"time\":\"2026-11-02T14:55:10Z\",\"level\":\"DEBUG\",\"msg\":\"GET /readyz\",\"status\":200,\"ms\":2}"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "describe shows why it restarted: three liveness checks timed out, and then the kubelet killed the container."
        },
        {
          "text": "To see what the old container was doing, add --previous to kubectl logs. These are the last lines it wrote before it froze.",
          "say": "To see what the old container was doing, add the previous flag to kubectl logs. These are the last lines it wrote before it froze."
        },
        {
          "text": "If a container keeps failing, its status becomes CrashLoopBackOff, and the kubelet waits longer before each new try, up to five minutes.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
