      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Last, the startup probe. Say a new release has migrations that take 40 seconds before the app can answer at all."
        },
        {
          "text": "With our startup probe, the kubelet checks every 2 seconds for up to a minute. At 40 seconds it passes, and the strict liveness checks begin.",
          "senses": {
            "minute": "time"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "Without it, liveness starts checking straight away. After about 30 seconds with no answer, it kills the container mid-migration, the next try starts over, and the pod never comes up."
        },
        {
          "text": "You could hold liveness back with initialDelaySeconds instead, but that's a fixed guess. The startup probe ends the moment the app is up.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mistakes",
