      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "To sum up, four mistakes to avoid."
        },
        {
          "text": "A liveness check that looks at the database, or any other service."
        },
        {
          "text": "No startup probe on an app that's slow to start."
        },
        {
          "text": "A timeout shorter than a slow but healthy answer, so a busy pod gets restarted."
        },
        {
          "text": "And the same check for liveness and readiness, so a pod that should just step aside gets restarted instead.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "next",
      "type": "title",
      "kicker": "Coming up",
      "title": "Episode 7: Logs",
      "subtitle": "Where they go, on-prem",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "So: startup waits for the app, liveness restarts a stuck process, and readiness decides who gets traffic."
        },
        {
          "text": "Rolling updates wait on readiness too, so a release that never gets ready never replaces the old pods."
        },
        {
          "text": "That restart left a question. The old container's logs were nearly gone. Next time: where logs actually live, and how to keep them.",
